 "_engagement": "11/10 v4 (coordinator; research 72 + 73): NO quiz framing. Each story opens on the claim as a concrete statement with the animal on screen, gives the reveal early (story 1 by ~0:11), then the why. The MYTH/TRUE board stamp is the reveal. No 'Myth or true?', no spoken countdowns. Two pause-and-reveal beats only (a 1.3 s '?' ring, no numbers): spiders fly and the headless roach. Story 1 is <= 30 s. Count + order + open loop at ~0:16 ('eight bug stories; the last one has no head', kept on screen as a chip until it pays off). Order: 4 busted, a midpoint re-hook ('Four stories down. The next four sound fake, and they're real.'), then 4 real, ending on the headless roach. A second loop (the girl with a spider in her mouth) opens at the midpoint and pays off in story 5. Every item ends on the next item's stake. Character beats every 30-40 s: Meatball's helmet (on at 0:06, off at 0:28, back on when spiders fly, kept at the end) and six roommate lines. Ending: callback to the opening, recap board, then 'watch this next' naming Kill It or Keep It. Narration avoids the channel's banned words.",
